(Two things compare field by field, and a list field compares by its
 contents, as two lists do: two new notes are the same, and they differ once
 one note's list holds something the other's does not.)

A thing called note has
  a text called title,
  a list called items.

a note called first.
a note called second.
If first is second then, Print "the same".
append "eggs" to first's items.
If first is not second then, Print "different once a list differs".
